---
name: site-qa-desk-check
description: >-
  Use when someone pastes a public website URL and wants it checked on desktop
  (1440px) and phone (390px): screenshots, sideways scroll, broken links,
  console errors and a ranked fix list. Also run by the weekly recheck routine.
---
# Site QA Desk - check one site

Input: one public URL (http/https; add https:// if missing). Optional: a page list from /workspace/site-qa-desk/siteqa-prefs.md. Limits: public pages only, at most 10 pages per run, at most 150 links checked, both viewports. Works with nothing connected.

## 1. Run the checker on your own computer
Use headless Chrome/Chromium via Playwright. Fixed paths: work folder `/workspace/site-qa-desk/`, script `/workspace/site-qa-desk/qa.js`, runs in `/workspace/site-qa-desk/qa-runs/`, prefs in `/workspace/site-qa-desk/siteqa-prefs.md`.

Install (once, robust):
```bash
mkdir -p /workspace/site-qa-desk && cd /workspace/site-qa-desk
[ -f package.json ] || npm init -y >/dev/null
npm i --prefix /workspace/site-qa-desk playwright-core@1 \
  || { npx -y playwright@1 install chromium; \
       P=$(find / -type d -name playwright-core -path '*node_modules*' 2>/dev/null | head -1); \
       [ -n "$P" ] && export NODE_PATH="$(dirname "$P")"; }
```
If the npm install fails, the fallback installs a Playwright Chromium and reuses any existing playwright-core it finds (via NODE_PATH).

Find Chrome: the script tries /usr/bin/google-chrome, /usr/bin/chromium, /usr/bin/chromium-browser, then the Playwright cache (~/.cache/ms-playwright). If none is found it runs `npx -y playwright@1 install chromium` and uses that build.

Write the script below to `/workspace/site-qa-desk/qa.js`, then run `cd /workspace/site-qa-desk && node qa.js <url> 10`. It crawls same-site links from the start page (skipping login, signup, account, admin, cart and checkout paths and files), loads each page at 1440x900 and 390x844 (phone user agent), saves top-of-page screenshots, measures sideways scroll (documentElement.scrollWidth vs clientWidth, plus the widest offending elements), records console errors, uncaught errors and failed requests, checks for a missing viewport tag, and checks every link it found (HEAD; any HEAD status of 400 or above is retried with GET before the link is called broken; one 15s retry on no response). It writes report.json plus PNGs to /workspace/site-qa-desk/qa-runs/<host>-<date>/, and copies screenshots of failed pages (load error, HTTP 400+, or blank) into qa-runs/<run>/failed/. If the 10-page or 150-link cap is hit, the report says so and how many pages or links were skipped.
If the user listed pages, run the script on each listed page with max 1 page instead of crawling (still 10 pages total).
If Chrome or Node is missing and cannot be installed, use your own browser at both sizes on the homepage and run the same checks in the page console; say which checks were skipped.

```js
// Site QA Desk check: node qa.js <url> [maxPages=10] [outDir]
const { chromium } = require('playwright-core');
const fs = require('fs'), path = require('path');
const start = Date.now();
const [,, rawUrl, maxArg, outArg] = process.argv;
const MAX = Math.min(parseInt(maxArg || '10', 10), 10);
const root = new URL(/^https?:\/\//.test(rawUrl) ? rawUrl : 'https://' + rawUrl);
const out = outArg || `/workspace/site-qa-desk/qa-runs/${root.hostname}-${new Date().toISOString().slice(0,16).replace(/[:T]/g,'-')}`;
fs.mkdirSync(out, { recursive: true });
const VIEWS = [{ name: 'desktop', width: 1440, height: 900 }, { name: 'mobile', width: 390, height: 844, isMobile: true, hasTouch: true }];
const cacheChrome = () => { const c = path.join(require('os').homedir(), '.cache/ms-playwright'); if (!fs.existsSync(c)) return;
  for (const d of fs.readdirSync(c).filter(d => /^chromium/.test(d)).sort().reverse()) for (const s of ['chrome-linux/chrome','chrome-linux64/chrome','chrome-linux/headless_shell','chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell']) { const p = path.join(c, d, s); if (fs.existsSync(p)) return p; } };
let exe = ['/usr/bin/google-chrome','/usr/bin/chromium','/usr/bin/chromium-browser'].find(p => fs.existsSync(p)) || cacheChrome();
if (!exe) { require('child_process').execSync('npx -y playwright@1 install chromium', { stdio: 'inherit' }); exe = cacheChrome(); }
const norm = u => { const x = new URL(u); x.hash = ''; return x.href; };
(async () => {
  const browser = await chromium.launch({ executablePath: exe, headless: true });
  const queue = [norm(root.href)], seen = new Set(queue), pages = [], allLinks = new Map();
  while (queue.length && pages.length < MAX) {
    const url = queue.shift(); const rec = { url, views: {} };
    for (const v of VIEWS) {
      const ctx = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: v.width, height: v.height }, isMobile: !!v.isMobile, hasTouch: !!v.hasTouch,
        userAgent: v.isMobile ? 'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 17_0 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/17.0 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1' : undefined });
      const p = await ctx.newPage(); const errs = [], failed = [];
      p.on('console', m => { if (m.type() === 'error') errs.push(m.text().slice(0, 200)); });
      p.on('pageerror', e => errs.push('Uncaught: ' + String(e.message).slice(0, 200)));
      p.on('requestfailed', r => failed.push(r.url().slice(0, 150) + ' (' + (r.failure()?.errorText || '') + ')'));
      const r = { status: null, errors: errs, failedRequests: failed };
      try {
        const resp = await p.goto(url, { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded', timeout: 20000 });
        await p.waitForLoadState('networkidle', { timeout: 5000 }).catch(() => {});
        r.status = resp ? resp.status() : null; r.finalUrl = p.url();
        Object.assign(r, await p.evaluate(() => {
          const de = document.documentElement, cw = de.clientWidth;
          const wide = [...document.querySelectorAll('body *')].filter(e => { const b = e.getBoundingClientRect(); return b.width > 0 && b.right > cw + 1 && getComputedStyle(e).position !== 'fixed'; })
            .slice(0, 5).map(e => e.tagName.toLowerCase() + (e.id ? '#' + e.id : '') + (e.className && typeof e.className === 'string' ? '.' + e.className.trim().split(/\s+/).slice(0,2).join('.') : '') + ` (right edge ${Math.round(e.getBoundingClientRect().right)}px)`);
          return { title: document.title, hasViewport: !!document.querySelector('meta[name=viewport]'), scrollWidth: de.scrollWidth, clientWidth: cw, overflowPx: Math.max(0, de.scrollWidth - cw), overflowEls: wide,
            textLen: document.body ? document.body.innerText.trim().length : 0,
            links: [...document.querySelectorAll('a[href]')].map(a => a.href).filter(h => /^https?:/.test(h)) };
        }));
        const shot = path.join(out, `${pages.length + 1}-${v.name}.png`);
        await p.screenshot({ path: shot, fullPage: false }); r.screenshot = shot;
        if (v.name === 'desktop') for (const l of r.links) {
          const n = norm(l); if (!allLinks.has(n)) allLinks.set(n, url);
          const lu = new URL(n);
          if (lu.host === root.host && !seen.has(n) && !/\.(pdf|jpe?g|png|gif|svg|zip|mp4|webp)$/i.test(lu.pathname) && !/(log-?in|sign-?in|sign-?up|register|account|admin|wp-admin|cart|checkout|logout|dashboard)/i.test(lu.pathname)) { seen.add(n); queue.push(n); }
        }
        delete r.links;
      } catch (e) { r.loadError = String(e.message).split('\n')[0]; const shot = path.join(out, `${pages.length + 1}-${v.name}.png`); await p.screenshot({ path: shot }).then(() => { r.screenshot = shot; }).catch(() => {}); }
      if (r.screenshot && (r.loadError || r.status >= 400 || r.textLen < 20)) { const fd = path.join(out, 'failed'); fs.mkdirSync(fd, { recursive: true }); fs.copyFileSync(r.screenshot, path.join(fd, path.basename(r.screenshot))); }
      rec.views[v.name] = r; await ctx.close();
    }
    pages.push(rec);
  }
  await browser.close();
  const pagesSkipped = queue.length, linksSkipped = Math.max(0, allLinks.size - 150);
  const links = [...allLinks.keys()].slice(0, 150), broken = [], blocked = [];
  const check = async u => { const ctl = AbortSignal.timeout(8000);
    try { let res = await fetch(u, { method: 'HEAD', redirect: 'follow', signal: ctl });
      if (res.status >= 400) res = await fetch(u, { method: 'GET', redirect: 'follow', signal: AbortSignal.timeout(8000) });
      if ([401, 403, 429, 999].includes(res.status)) blocked.push({ u, s: res.status }); else if (res.status >= 400) broken.push({ u, s: res.status, on: allLinks.get(u) });
    } catch (e) { try { const r2 = await fetch(u, { method: 'GET', redirect: 'follow', signal: AbortSignal.timeout(15000) }); if (r2.status >= 400 && ![401,403,429,999].includes(r2.status)) broken.push({ u, s: r2.status, on: allLinks.get(u) }); } catch (e2) { broken.push({ u, s: 'no response', on: allLinks.get(u) }); } } };
  for (let i = 0; i < links.length; i += 10) await Promise.all(links.slice(i, i + 10).map(check));
  const fixes = [];
  for (const pg of pages) for (const [vn, r] of Object.entries(pg.views)) {
    if (r.loadError) fixes.push([1, `${pg.url} (${vn}): could not load - ${r.loadError}`]);
    else if (r.status >= 400) fixes.push([1, `${pg.url} (${vn}): returns HTTP ${r.status}`]);
    else if (r.textLen < 20) fixes.push([1, `${pg.url} (${vn}): page renders almost no text - possible blank page`]);
    if (r.overflowPx > 0) fixes.push([vn === 'mobile' ? 2 : 3, `${pg.url} (${vn}): sideways scroll, page is ${r.overflowPx}px wider than the screen. Widest: ${r.overflowEls.join(', ') || 'n/a'}`]);
    if (r.errors?.length) fixes.push([3, `${pg.url} (${vn}): ${r.errors.length} console error(s), first: ${r.errors[0]}`]);
    if (vn === 'mobile' && r.hasViewport === false) fixes.push([2, `${pg.url}: no <meta name="viewport"> tag, so phones show a zoomed-out desktop page`]);
    if (r.title === '') fixes.push([5, `${pg.url}: empty <title>`]);
  }
  for (const b of broken) fixes.push([internal(b.u) ? 2 : 4, `Broken link ${b.u} -> ${b.s} (found on ${b.on})`]);
  function internal(u) { return new URL(u).host === root.host; }
  const dedup = [...new Map(fixes.map(f => [f[1].replace(/ \((desktop|mobile)\)/, ''), f])).values()].sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]);
  const secs = ((Date.now() - start) / 1000).toFixed(1);
  const caps = []; if (pagesSkipped) caps.push(`${MAX}-page cap hit: ${pagesSkipped} more page(s) found but skipped`); if (linksSkipped) caps.push(`150-link cap hit: ${linksSkipped} link(s) skipped`);
  const res = { site: root.href, pagesChecked: pages.length, pagesSkipped, linksChecked: links.length, linksSkipped, caps, broken, blocked, fixes: dedup.map(f => `P${f[0]} ${f[1]}`), seconds: +secs, pages };
  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(out, 'report.json'), JSON.stringify(res, null, 2));
  console.log(`SITE: ${root.href}  pages: ${pages.length}  links checked: ${links.length}  time: ${secs}s  out: ${out}`);
  for (const pg of pages) { const d = pg.views.desktop, m = pg.views.mobile;
    console.log(`- ${pg.url} | ${d.loadError ? 'LOAD FAIL' : d.status} | overflow 1440:${d.overflowPx ?? '?'}px 390:${m.overflowPx ?? '?'}px | console errs ${(d.errors||[]).length}/${(m.errors||[]).length}`); }
  caps.forEach(c => console.log('CAP: ' + c));
  console.log(`Broken links: ${broken.length}  Unverifiable (bot-blocked): ${blocked.length}`);
  console.log('FIX LIST:'); (res.fixes.length ? res.fixes : ['none - all checks passed']).forEach((f, i) => console.log(`${i + 1}. ${f}`));
})();
```

## 2. Look before you report
Open the homepage screenshots (1440 and 390) and any page that failed (qa-runs/<run>/failed/). Confirm with your own eyes: blank or black hero, text cut off, overlapping or unreadable elements, a cookie banner covering the page. Add what you see to the fix list; drop anything the screenshot shows is a false alarm. Links answering 401/403/429/999 are "could not verify (site blocks bots)", never "broken". A page that would not load is "could not load", never PASS.

## 3. Rank the fixes
P1 page down, error status, or blank. P2 phone problems (sideways scroll at 390px, missing viewport tag) and broken links on the same site. P3 console errors and desktop sideways scroll. P4 broken links to other sites. P5 cosmetic (empty title). Within a level, homepage first. Each fix is one plain line: what, where, the likely cause (e.g. "div.hero is 608px wide on a 390px screen - set max-width:100%"), never a guess stated as fact.

## 4. Output (one screen, verdict first)
```
VERDICT: 2 things to fix (1 on phones)   - 10 pages, 150 links, 38s
[homepage 1440px screenshot] [homepage 390px screenshot]
Sideways scroll: none at 1440 / 1 page at 390
Broken links: 1 (list)   Could not verify: 0
Console errors: 0 pages
Caps: none (or: "10-page cap hit, 7 pages skipped" / "150-link cap hit, 42 links skipped")
FIX LIST
1. P2 ...
2. P4 ...
```
If everything passes, say "All clear" and still show both screenshots. If report.json has a non-empty `caps` list, always state each cap and the skipped count.

## 5. Save and baseline
Keep /workspace/site-qa-desk/qa-runs/<host>-<date>/report.json, the PNGs and failed/. Baseline: if no baseline exists for this host, copy this run's report.json to /workspace/site-qa-desk/qa-runs/<host>-baseline.json and record its path under the site in /workspace/site-qa-desk/siteqa-prefs.md. This is the only place a baseline is saved. When a previous run exists for the same site, add a short "Since last check: new / fixed / still open" section by comparing fix lists.

Read-only: never log in, type passwords, submit forms, click buy/sign-up buttons, or change a site, repository or hosting setting. Public pages only, max 10 pages per run.
